  "command": "make bench-prefix",
  "methodology": "Open-loop burst through EngineCore on CUDA bf16. 8 requests arrive together at t=0. Each prompt is one shared 512-token prefix plus a 32-token tail; the first tail token is the request index, so two tails cannot collide and share a block past the prefix. max_new_tokens is 8, max_batch is 8, block size is 16. The pool is max_batch times one request's reserve-max budget, so the cache-off run fits without a rejection and the cache-on run is not faster merely because the cold run would not fit. One warmup replay of each mode is discarded. 5 timed repetitions alternate which mode runs first. Each replay builds a new pool, so the cache starts empty and the first request is always a miss. TTFT is the replayer's stamp, arrival to the first generated token, taken at the end of that request's prefill and before the step decodes. p50 and p99 are nearest-rank over the requests in one replay. The reported TTFT is the median of those p50s, with the min and max. Prefill tokens scored are all 544 prompt tokens of every request with the cache off, and query tokens minus hit tokens with it on. A hit still gathers the cached pages to score the tail. The skipped work is the prefix's projections and MLP. Clocks are not locked. The card also drives the display. Host is WSL2. HTTP is not in these numbers.",
